The R22 v3-poller round pinned the php_grf reset image flip to 1.2207s,
13ms after rockchip-drm binds fdd90000.vop + fde20000.dsi. Disable the
whole display family so the boot is headless; if the DBG30 CON0 flip
banner no longer appears and eth0 open survives, the display bring-up
(VOP2 vendor-handoff path, DSI2 controller, or the OOT panel driver)
owns the php_grf reset and the GMAC read wedge.
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-topeet.dts | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-topeet.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-topeet.dts
index 5405342bf..69a222236 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-topeet.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-topeet.dts
@@ -974,3 +974,25 @@ touchscreen@14 {
 		status = "okay";
 	};
 };
+
+/* TEMP 0031 (headless discriminator round): disable the whole display
+ * pipeline (VOP2 + its MMU + DSI2 + DCPHY + the panel beneath dsi0) to
+ * test whether the ~1.22s php_grf reset event — which lands ~13ms after
+ * rockchip-drm binds VOP+DSI — is caused by the display bring-up path.
+ * Judgment instrument: the DBG30 poller's serial CON0-flip banner.
+ */
+&vop {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&vop_mmu {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&mipidcphy0 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&dsi0 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
